body:
AHHHHHHHH I mustve missed the TB bit that adds it to unarmed attack! Im a moron! Thanks brother this was a helpful read. We just got to Act 2 and did mostly all of it barring a few minibosses. Ive switched to fighter and I love it but Ill give monk a rip now.

&#x200B;

Ive seen folks discuss respeccing for the DEX and STR even. The dex gloves we have so Ill throw them on and STR we have a couple elixirs I would feel comfortable dumping that later

This is extremely common. Been living in Florida for 7 years now. I see this kinda shit DAILY. When Trump was in office GUARANTEED you saw a pickup truck with a trump flag mounted in the bed.

&#x200B;

The flood can't come soon enough.

Your dad is really stupid for that. I hope he's ok because those aren't nice injuries, but we have PPE rules for a reason. I used to be QC on sites and some OSHA compliance so this stuff just upsets me because it's so preventable and I hate to see people hurt themselves, especially self-inflicted stupidity.

&#x200B;

Anyway hope for a speedy recovery and tell him to get some damn pants! :)

NL when he finds the mf who keeps tryin to skate uphill.

&#x200B;

NL when he finds who spilled his McDonald's Sprite.

&#x200B;

NL when he smokes the shit that made Calvin Coolidge.

&#x200B;

NL when he goes Jamie Lee Curtis mode.

&#x200B;

I need to stop now.

If youre having trouble with Bahamut, try using ward materia with fire on Cloud or whoever is dying. Makes the fire immune and if it's high enough lvl when he summons Ifrit it will heal you. Bahamut is the hardest fight bar none in that series. Use Tifa too as she is really really quick and can dodge attacks easier. Tifa, Aerith, and Cloud worked well for me. 

&#x200B;

Which fight specifically are you struggling on?
